ent is horizontal. Therefore, we require ${y}^{′}(t)=0$ while ${x}^{′}(t)\\ne 0.$\n\nSo, we first find the derivatives of $x$ and $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=7,\\,{y}^{′}(t)=9{t}^{2}-18.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving ${y}^{′}(t)=0$ gives\n\n$$\n9({t}^{2}-2)=0\\,⟹\\,t=\\pm \\sqrt{2}.\n$$\n\nNow, we note that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(-\\sqrt{2}) & =7\\ne 0, \\\\ {x}^{′}(\\sqrt{2}) & =7\\ne 0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich confirms that the normal to the curve is indeed vertical when $t=\\pm \\sqrt{2}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186523029 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "33356aae-e56a-5b04-9377-c9bf2dc3b354" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{29\\pi}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523034}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "33356aae-e56a-5b04-9377-c9bf2dc3b354" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{29\\pi}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523034} :answer-field/id #uuid "9884991f-b474-5bed-ac12-6297bbde8db8" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523055} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06b5663f-ab15-59a8-aa75-83c593f9fcb2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{47\\pi}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523020}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "06b5663f-ab15-59a8-aa75-83c593f9fcb2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{47\\pi}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523020} :answer-field/id #uuid "aca313d6-1360-5578-942b-e8db280a47a5" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523063} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "24556c01-0a33-5acf-b303-408270710678" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{35\\pi}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523030}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "24556c01-0a33-5acf-b303-408270710678" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.t